---
title: Vanilla Sponge
serves: 1
---

= Preparation

Coat a #cake pan{} with a light film of @fat{} and line it with a #parchment circle{}.

= Vanilla Sponge

Blend the @butter{65%g}(melted) with the @vanilla extract{7.5%g}.

Combine the @eggs{192.5%g}, @egg yolks{65%g}, and @sugar{192.5%g} in a #mixer bowl{}. Set over a #pan{} of barely simmering @water{} and whisk constantly until the sugar dissolves and the mixture reaches 43°C.

Transfer to the #mixer{} and whip on high speed with the whip attachment until the foam reaches maximum volume. Reduce the speed to medium and mix for ~{15%minutes} to stabilize the mixture.

Turn off the mixer and fold in the sifted @flour{192.5%g}(all-purpose). Temper the butter mixture with a small portion of the batter and fold into the larger portion of batter.

Scale 450 g of batter into the prepared #cake pan{}, filling the pan two-thirds full.

Bake in the #oven{} at 177°C until the top of the cake springs back when lightly touched, about ~{30%minutes}.

Cool the cake in the pan for ~{5%minutes}, then unmold onto a #sheet pan{} lined with #parchment paper{} that is dusted with #confectioners' sugar{} to cool completely.

> Chocolate Sponge Variation

> Replace 27.5 g of the all-purpose flour with @Dutch-process cocoa powder{27.5%g}. 

> Sift the cocoa powder together with the flour. 

> Follow the remaining method as stated above.